TEXT -184 208 Left 5 ;Example 10KV Breaker
TEXT -64 280 Left 2 ;snubber resistance\nsnubber capacitance\noperating voltage
TEXT -184 544 Left 2 ;Working of the breaker model:\n=============================\n \nThis is an example for a high voltage breaker\nThe breaker is intended to clear the circuit at about current zero\nTherefore there are only small voltage spikes at the now opened circuit\nThe breaker uses also snubber resistance and capacitance between\nthe breaker poles to prevent higher voltage spikes\nThere are also two movs(varistors) at each side of the breaker\nagain to prevent high overvoltages.\n \nHow the switching at current ~zero is done:\n===========================================\nIf the breaker ctrl pin goes to zero (switching off order)\nthe current is measured and if ioff0 is reached a oszillator\nwith high frequency is started to get many simulation breakpoints\nSince now the current measurement can be with finer resolution\nthe breaker waits till the much smaller ioff value is reached\nand the switcher wents into off state.
TEXT -64 320 Left 2 ;Set td1 to about 10ms to see the output voltage with finer resolution\nBut note: This will slow down the simulation\nioff and ioff0 see text below\nexp parameter from mov 9 should be ok\ncbrk parameter for the oszillator circuit\nset cbrk lower to get higher resolution\nBut note: This will slow down simulation
